\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.5}{\ignorespaces The flow field blowup at $t \approx \qty {13}{\second }$. The vectors show the emergence of non-physical motions caused by the failure to preserve the hydrostatic balance. The displacement of the particles further creates spurious forces, leading to breakdown. Both figures also capture a reflection of the spurious wave at the top boundary.}}{87}{figure.caption.88}\protected@file@percent }
